    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thx. also, sometimes we find these really weird edge cases where the screen reader just skips certain elements or the focus ring disappears entirely on specific mobile browsers. what's the best way to audit for those kinds of hidden accessibility bugs?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For these edge cases, build your audit around manual testing sessions using multiple assistive technologies like VoiceOver or NVDA across different iOS and Android browsers. You should also consider recruiting real people with disabilities to interact with your prototype in their natural environment, as simulated reports often miss context-specific failures. Finally, ensure your CSS doesn't collapse focus outlines by default for custom elements, and treat focus rings as absolute design requirements.",
      "source": "target",
